WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.560
Step three of our compression skills is rate and rhythm.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:06.220
To keep blood moving effectively to the brain,

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.560
you need to maintain a rate

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:10.880
of 100 to 120 compressions per minute.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.280
Now, in a high-stress situation,

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.940
it can be really hard to judge exactly how fast that is.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.080
A great trick is to use music.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.040
You've probably heard people mention songs

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.480
like Stayin' Alive or Baby Shark.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:24.920
Any song with a steady beat

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:29.080
between 100 and 120 beats per minute works perfectly.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.600
Counting out loud from one to 30 as you work

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.240
also helps you stay on track

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.480
and keeps everyone around you informed of your progress.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.200
As you push at this speed,

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:42.320
there is one more vital step, full chest recoil.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.119
Recoil simply means release.

00:00:45.119 --> 00:00:47.119
After every single push down,

00:00:47.119 --> 00:00:48.880
you must lift your hands just enough

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.279
to let the chest spring all the way back up

00:00:51.279 --> 00:00:52.880
to its normal position.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.919
Think of it like squeezing a sponge.

00:00:54.919 --> 00:00:56.619
You squeeze to push the water out,

00:00:56.619 --> 00:00:58.160
but you have to let go completely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.880
to let the sponge expand so it can soak up more water.

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:03.840
The heart works in a similar way.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.480
If you don't let the chest come all the way back up,

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.839
the heart doesn't have time to refill with blood,

00:01:08.839 --> 00:01:12.160
and your next compression won't have anything to pump out.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:13.360
Watch your instructor now

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.360
as they demonstrate a full set of 30 compressions.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.160
Pay attention to that steady rhythm

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:21.760
and how the chest fully resets between every single push.

